                -- two defects. (1) STACKED PULLS: every event scheduled a\
                -- blind task.delay(2) clear, so pull A at t=0 cleared the\
                -- flag at t=2 even though pull B at t=1.5 owned the window\
                -- until t=3.5 - the autoparry un-skipped while the pull was\
                -- still live. Each event now bumps a generation counter and\
                -- a delayed clear only lands if its captured generation is\
                -- still the live one (the same latch-safe shape as the\
                -- ratchet work). (2) SLOW SYNC: the flag reached the\
                -- autoparry gate only through the 0.2s poll loop below, so\
                -- the skip arrived up to 200ms into the pull and lingered\
                -- 200ms past it; the listener now writes the gate state\
                -- directly (ON here, OFF in the generation-safe clear) and\
                -- the poll loop stays purely as a redundant backstop.\
